vf:biosensing-interface a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Biosensing Interface"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Physical sensor hardware system that detects physiological signals such as heart rate, electroencephalography (EEG), galvanic skin response (GSR), and electromyography (EMG) to enable real-time adaptation of virtual interaction and user experience. Biosensing interfaces bridge human physiology and computational systems, translating biological measurements into actionable digital feedback for [[Affective Computing]] and [[Human-Robot Interaction]] applications."@en ;
