    rdfs:comment "3D Graphics Standards are technical specifications and conventions governing the representation, rendering, and interchange of three-dimensional visual data, including APIs like [[OpenGL]], [[DirectX]], and [[Vulkan]], shader languages, and coordinate system conventions. These standards ensure consistency in visual output across platforms and enable developers to create graphics pipelines compatible with diverse hardware architectures."@en ;
