vf:economic-layer a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Economic Layer"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The EconomicLayer represents the abstraction level of implemented economic mechanisms, incentive structures, market designs, resource allocation systems, and game-theoretic implementations that govern economic behavior in blockchain and distributed systems. This layer encompasses concrete economic implementations including token emission schedules (Bitcoin's halving schedule, Ethereum's changing issuance policy), fee market implementations (EIP-1559's base fee adjustment mechanism, priority fee auctions), incentive mechanism implementations (mining reward distribution, staking yield calculations, validator reward formulas), penalty mechanisms (slashing implementations specifying exact penalty amounts and conditions), market mechanism implementations (automated market maker formulas, bonding curves, liquidity pool mechanics), resource pricing mechanisms (gas price mechanisms, storage rent, computation pricing), economic security implementations (cost-of-attack calculations, security budget allocations), and game-theoretic mechanism implementations (auction mechanisms, voting systems, coordination games). Unlike ConceptualLayer which addresses abstract economic principles and theorie"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf vf:infrastructure ;
    vc:authorityScore "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:maturity "draft" ;
    vc:qualityScore "0.35"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:slug "economic-layer" ;
    vc:sourceDomain "infrastructure" .

vf:education-and-ai a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Education and AI"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Education and AI (Artificial Intelligence in Education, AIED) denotes the deployment of machine-learning systems—intelligent tutoring systems (ITS) such as Carnegie Learning Mathia at 600K+ US students across 1,500+ districts, ALEKS at 25M+ cumulative users since 1996, Knewton (acquired Wiley 2019 for ~$17M after raising $157M), Squirrel AI at 5M+ K-12 Chinese students across 4,000+ centres in 700+ cities; conversational AI tutors built on large language models such as Khan Academy Khanmigo (GPT-4) at 1M+ students across 90+ districts free to US/Canada teachers from August 2024, Synthesis Tutor ($35M Series A 2024, Andreessen Horowitz) at $35/month family plan, Mathpresso QANDA at 90M+ users across 50+ countries, Brilliant.org at 10M+ active learners, MagicSchool AI at 4M+ educators across 6,000+ US schools with 80+ teacher tools at $99/teacher/year; generative-AI assistants (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini) used by 26% of US teens 13-17 for schoolwork per Pew Research 2024 (up from 13% in 2023) and 70% of teens for any generative AI per Common Sense Media 2024; AI grading and integrity tooling (Gradescope at 2,600+ universities processing 100M+ submissions reducing grading time 70%, Turni"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <urn:visionflow:linked:applied-ai>,
        <urn:visionflow:linked:conversational-ai-applications>,
        <urn:visionflow:linked:human-centred-ai>,
        vf:educational-technology ;
    vc:authorityScore "0.87"^^xsd:float ;
    vc:enables <urn:visionflow:linked:accessibility-provisioning>,
        <urn:visionflow:linked:differentiated-instruction>,
